0a9a348","solve/summary.json":"9b1606d96da80d055d248d1fb461218206d279794c0759466d9377d8ec6a358a"},"feedback_items":[{"id":"F1","text":"Centralize strict scalar validation in the generator API scaffold **(top shared change)\n\n**Symptom.** Well-tested generators can accept `bool`, integral `float`, numeric\n`str`, negative sample indexes, and non-string difficulty values because callers\nreach `gen_ctx` before task-local validation. This review found the same class in\nthree places: the repaired target had 33 findings before its local fix;\n`7a15f5e5ebd9` has 108; `c5309d8fa84c` has 112. Evidence:\n`checks/before/checks/55993f4c12af_before_defect_lint.log`,\n`checks/audit/7a15f5e5ebd9-battery/checks/7a15f5e5ebd9_audit_defect_lint.log`, and\n`checks/audit/c5309d8fa84c-battery/checks/c5309d8fa84c_audit_defect_lint.log`.\n\n**Suggested change.** Add a public shared helper used by new-generator scaffolds,\nfor example `validate_generate_call(seed, sample_index, difficulty, overrides,\naxes)`, with exact-type checks before any coercion or draw. Make the default\ncontract reject unknown keys, `bool` for integer/color axes, non-integral types,\nnegative indexes, and invalid difficulty tokens. Keep task-specific range and\ncombination checks local. Add one portable conformance test generator to ensure\nfuture changes to `gen_ctx` cannot reintroduce coercion. Existing generators can\nmigrate incrementally; the detector already provides the inventory."},{"id":"F2","text":"Provide a reusable finite parametric-episode audit harness\n\n**Symptom.** A sound parametric proposal currently needs repeated task-local code\nfor seed-to-setting coverage, exact Racket execution, canonical parity,\ndemonstration-only survivor checks, private/public serialization, runtime/source\nreceipts, and negative ambiguity canaries. The working implementation under\n`generators/55993f4c12af/workspace/parametric/prototype.py` demonstrates the\npattern but necessarily duplicates infrastructure that future agents would likely\ncopy and subtly weaken.\n\n**Suggested change.** Add a small helper in the reviewer runtime that accepts a\nfinite `settings` sequence, `emit_program(setting)`, an input sampler, canonical\ndefault, and episode sizes. It should materialize source-bound private/public\nJSONL, execute all labels and rivals through protected Racket, refuse overwrite,\ncheck demo-only uniqueness, and preserve failed rows. Task-local code would still\ndefine the meaningful parameters and input contract. The retained 27-setting\naudit in `checks/parametric/run-01/` is a concrete fixture for the helper's tests."}],"packet_id":"78f0415abaad620af8aed8e83e5a0404e7f1b427e46f3acb367636e0fdfd2881","reviewer_blind_solve":{"attempt_count":1,"attempt_intents":{"solve-blind/attempts/0001/report.json":"solve"},"attempt_reports":["solve-blind/attempts/0001/report.json"],"earlier_rule_exposure":"no","feedback_policy":"visible_only","generator_hash":"66c20ab0c44e2199caf1664e2b994fa55462fe3383efcb6addc2085b8c7fbbff","instance_hash":"46bb0101c0a2330eafec1c1c962ed65ea2a08673d296396efa322b371b8d1e0e","reference_consulted_during_solve":false,"solve_kind":"blind_before_repair","source_kind":"reviewer_authored","status":"finished","task_id":"cde6cd1740f9"},"reviewer_solve":{"attempt_count":1,"attempt_intents":{"solve/attempts/0001/report.json":"solve"},"attempt_reports":["solve/attempts/0001/report.json"],"earlier_rule_exposure":"yes","feedback_policy":"visible_only","generator_hash":"1d38b983e4c7edb9d70d6bfec9877d5b631e4583a1398b8c8383a1d7f0a9a348","instance_hash":"4a9f4b25368f2935a2decc3f82a779c2cafd0a939287c47af0af7e77a822b60e","reference_consulted_during_solve":false,"source_kind":"reviewer_authored","status":"finished"},"schema":"arcpuzzles-review-intake-v1","stopping_reason":"Selected repair, parametric proposal, visible solves, required checks, lesson diagnostics, and both assigned audits are complete. Audit-only defects remain documented and were not modified.","task_id":"55993f